ellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- Norvane Utilities plans spending up 12%, including a C$450M tender due in Q2 2027.\n- VLTX won 60% of the last tender round. Its utility order intake has risen for four straight quarters, from C$610M in 2025Q4 to C$670M in 2026Q3.\n- The quarterly gain has narrowed from about C$30M to about C$15M.\n- The capital plans are filed intentions, and the tenders are not yet awarded. I don't know whether the 2027 tenders are larger than the last round.\n\n**Data centres (rising, but slowing)**\n- Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, which is slower than in 2026. Power availability is limiting new sites.\n- The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres make up 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months.\n- I found no direct figure for equipment orders from data centres. Those long waits could mean actual orders lag the growth in requests.\n\nI haven't weighted the two buyers by their share of VLTX orders. I also haven't checked the debt and equity financing findings from n3's sub-nodes (n7, n8), which bear on whether utilities can fund their plans.\n\nSources are the n5 and n6 results, from sub-nodes I opened for the utility and data-centre questions: n5.r1 and n6.r1.","ttft_ms":1796,"type":"result","duration_ms":50683,"uuid":"1db56589-33e8-401e-aea4-2c118abbb76e","ttft_stream_ms":798,"time_to_request_ms":103,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":11,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":23,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":3,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":3,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":3,"time